<p></p>
<h1 id=3D"CurrencyConversionforPricebooks-SalesforceCurrencyConversionPlan:=
">Salesforce Currency Conversion Plan:</h1>
<p>Marc=E2=80=99s original write up link: <a class=3D"external-link" data-c=
ard-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"https://helpsystemsllc.sharepoint.com/:w:=
/r/sites/PROJ-LoBOperationalReadinessTransformation/_layouts/15/Doc.aspx?so=
urcedoc=3D%7B2781373B-1ACD-4C7A-AE86-422649B7FB38%7D&amp;file=3DFortra%20Re=
vised%20Multi-Currency%20Approach%20Summary.docx&amp;fromShare=3Dtrue&amp;a=
ction=3Ddefault&amp;mobileredirect=3Dtrue" rel=3D"nofollow">https://helpsys=
temsllc.sharepoint.com/:w:/r/sites/PROJ-LoBOperationalReadinessTransformati=
on/_layouts/15/Doc.aspx?sourcedoc=3D%7B2781373B-1ACD-4C7A-AE86-422649B7FB38=
%7D&amp;file=3DFortra%20Revised%20Multi-Currency%20Approach%20Summary.docx&=
amp;fromShare=3Dtrue&amp;action=3Ddefault&amp;mobileredirect=3Dtrue</a></p>
<p>Salesforce Documentation: <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://hel=
psystemsllc.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/DEPT-BusinessSystems2/Shared%20Docum=
ents/BSI%20Hub/Currency%20Conversion%20in%20Salesforce%20AutoFX_User_Guide_=
v1_3.pdf?csf=3D1&amp;web=3D1&amp;e=3Dy3FO0o" rel=3D"nofollow">Currency Conv=
ersion in Salesforce AutoFX_User_Guide_v1_3.pdf</a></p>
<p><strong>Multi-Currency Implementation Recommendation</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Executive Summary</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Based on extensive research and analysis of Salesforce Revenue Cloud cap=
abilities, we can confirm the workability and integrity of Fortra=E2=80=99s=
 desired approach: Single Currency Per Transaction with Native Multi-Curren=
cy Support. This approach aligns with Revenue Cloud's native architecture w=
hile meeting Fortra's requirements for USD-based pricing formulas and multi=
-currency profitability calculations.&nbsp;</p>
<p>This solution allows Fortra to maintain USD as the basis for profitabili=
ty calculations while presenting and transacting in customer currencies, wi=
th automatic flow through the entire Revenue Cloud lifecycle from Quote to =
Asset to Invoice.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Single Currency Per Transaction Approach</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Core Architecture</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Enable Salesforce Multi-Currency with USD as the corporate currency.&nbs=
p;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Store all transactions in the customer's preferred currency (EUR, GBP, C=
AD, etc.) as additional price book entries for each product in relevant pri=
ce books.&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Use native Revenue Cloud currency fields that automatically flow through=
 the quote-to-cash lifecycle.&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>During Quoting, prices in the selected Quote currency will be pulled fro=
m the selected price book and used for product pricing and Quote and Quote =
Line related calculations.&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Leverage Salesforce's built-in currency conversion for reporting and pro=
fitability analysis.&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>How USD-Based Pricing Formulas Work in This Approach</strong>&nb=
sp;</p>
<p>The USD-based pricing formulas that Fortra requires are applied at the p=
roduct/pricebook level, NOT during the quoting process. This is a critical =
distinction that ensures clean data flow through Revenue Cloud:&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Product Setup Phase:</strong><code>&nbsp;</code></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Define master price in USD <code>&nbsp;</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Create pricebook entries for each currency using Fortra=E2=80=99s conver=
sion formulas<code>&nbsp;</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>Example: USD $1,000 =E2=86=92 EUR =E2=82=AC920, GBP =C2=A3840, CAD $1,35=
0<code>&nbsp;</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>These converted prices are stored as static values in pricebook entries&=
nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quoting Phase:</strong><code>&nbsp;</code></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Quote inherits currency from Opportunity (e.g., EUR)<code>&nbsp;</code><=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Revenue Cloud automatically selects the EUR pricebook entries<code>&nbsp=
;</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>The =E2=82=AC920 price is used directly - NO conversion happens at quote=
 time<code>&nbsp;</code></p></li>
<li>
<p>This EUR value is stored in native fields and flows through the entire l=
ifecycle&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Pricebook Entry Management</strong>&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<p>On an ongoing basis, pricebook entries for additional currencies will be=
 populated using one of two methods:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Automated Method</strong>: The "Create New Products" flow will a=
pply USD-based prices to formulas provided by Fortra for each currency to a=
utomatically generate pricebook entries for each supported currency. The co=
nversion from USD master price to local currency happens at this point, not=
 during quoting&nbsp;<span style=3D"background-color: rgb(254,222,200);">(W=
hat about bulk add products?)</span></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Manual Method</strong>: Pricebook entries can also be manually c=
reated and updated for each currency&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p><strong>Quote Creation Process</strong>&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Quote inherits currency from the Opportunity (customer's preferred curre=
ncy)&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Revenue Cloud automatically selects pricebook entries matching the Quote=
 currency&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>The currency-specific price from the pricebook entry is used directly (n=
o conversion at quote time)&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>These values are stored in native Revenue Cloud fields and flow through =
the entire lifecycle&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Currency is locked after Quote creation to maintain pricing integrity&nb=
sp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>If the Sales Representative desires to switch the currency for a Quote, =
a new opportunity in the desired currency will need to be created, and a ne=
w Quote for that Opportunity will need to be created.&nbsp; The new Quote w=
ill inherit the new Opportunities currency.&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p><strong>Lifecycle Flow</strong>&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<p>The native Revenue Cloud fields will automatically flow through the enti=
re lifecycle:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Quote (EUR) =E2=86=92 Order (EUR) =E2=86=92 Asset (EUR) =E2=86=92 Invoic=
e (EUR)&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>All native currency fields maintain the customer's currency throughout&n=
bsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>No custom field cascade required&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Asset-based ordering (amendments, renewals) works seamlessly&nbsp;</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Revenue recognition maintains transaction-time values&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<ol start=3D"4">
<li>
<p><strong>Profitability Calculations</strong>&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Revenue tracked in customer currency using native fields&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Profitability calculations use CURRENCYRATE() function to convert custom=
er currency total to USD corporate currency&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Net profitability displayed in USD (via conversion)&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Executive dashboards and reports show all values normalized to USD for c=
omparison&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key Benefits of This Approach</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Works with Revenue Cloud's native architecture - no fighting the platfor=
m&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Values flow automatically through the entire quote-to-cash lifecycle&nbs=
p;</p></li>
<li>
<p>No cascade of custom fields required across Quote, Order, Asset, and Inv=
oice objects&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Asset-based ordering remains fully functional for amendments and renewal=
s&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Historical exchange rates preserved at transaction time&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Compliant with ASC 606 revenue recognition requirements&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Simplified maintenance - no custom field synchronization needed&nbsp;</p=
></li>
<li>
<p>Native reporting capabilities work without modification&nbsp;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Performance optimized - no formula field calculations at runtime&nbsp;</=
p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Critical Considerations</strong>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Once multi-currency is enabled in Salesforce, it cannot be disabled&nbsp=
;</p></li>
<li>
<p>Exchange rates must be maintained regularly in Salesforce setup&nbsp;</p=
></li>
<li>
<p>All users will see currency ISO codes (EUR, GBP, etc.) before amounts<co=
de>&nbsp;</code><br>
&nbsp;</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
